From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000028
Subject: [PATCH] vending: population shells' stalls can be listed in the vending tables

0001 kept a shell's stall out of `vendings` / `vending_items`, which makes it
invisible to anything that searches those tables (a script or mod). The new
battle flag population_engine_list_stalls (conf/battle/population_engine.conf,
off by default, so nothing changes unless a mod or the server owner turns it on,
for instance with setbattleflag) writes a shell's stall like a player's.

A shell's cart has no cart_inventory rows, so its `cartinventory_id` holds the
item id with the top bit set (0x80000000 | nameid); a player's rows are unchanged.
Closing a stall and every sale always clean up, so turning the flag off leaves no
rows behind. Shells are never `autotrade`, so restoring autotraders ignores them,
and the tables are emptied at map-server start as before.

--- a/src/custom/battle_config_init.inc
+++ b/src/custom/battle_config_init.inc
@@ -74,3 +74,4 @@
 { "population_engine_loot_timeout_ms",&battle_config.population_engine_loot_timeout_ms,15000,1000,600000,},
 { "population_engine_loot_radius",&battle_config.population_engine_loot_radius,9,1,20,},
 { "population_engine_loot_hp_abort_pct",&battle_config.population_engine_loot_hp_abort_pct,30,0,100,},
+{ "population_engine_list_stalls",&battle_config.population_engine_list_stalls,0,0,1,},
--- a/src/custom/battle_config_struct.inc
+++ b/src/custom/battle_config_struct.inc
@@ -150,3 +150,6 @@
 int32 population_engine_loot_radius;
 /// Below this HP% a shell stops going for even rare drops mid-fight.
 int32 population_engine_loot_hp_abort_pct;
+/// 1 = a shell's vending stall and buying store are also written to the vendings / vending_items and
+/// buyingstores / buyingstore_items tables, so a script or mod can search them. 0 = memory only, as before.
+int32 population_engine_list_stalls;
--- a/src/map/vending.cpp
+++ b/src/map/vending.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,17 @@
 static uint32 vending_nextid = 0; ///Vending_id counter
 static DBMap *vending_db; ///DB holder the vender : charid -> map_session_data
 
+/// Key of a cart slot in `vending_items`.`cartinventory_id`. A population shell's cart lives in memory
+/// only, so its slots have no cart_inventory id; the item id is stored instead with the top bit set, so
+/// a search of the table (e.g. a @whosell script) can still tell what the shell sells.
+static uint32 vending_item_key( const map_session_data& sd, int32 idx ){
+	if( IS_POPULATION_ENGINE_ACCOUNT_ID(sd.status.account_id) ){
+		const t_itemid nameid = sd.cart.u.items_cart[idx].nameid; // packed: copy out
+		return 0x80000000u | static_cast<uint32>(nameid);
+	}
+	return sd.cart.u.items_cart[idx].id;
+}
+
 //Autotrader
 static DBMap *vending_autotrader_db; /// Holds autotrader info: char_id -> struct s_autotrader
 static void vending_autotrader_remove(struct s_autotrader *at, bool remove);
